  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IWRM 4 WASH A Market-based Approach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inception phaseIn year one (October 2019-July 2021), the project will undertake a number of activities geared towards setting a strong foundation for effective project implementation. Key activities that will be prioritized during this phase include defining the project scope and gaining stakeholder consensus; developing a detailed implementation plan with the key strategic partners, conducting a baseline assessment to establish the project benchmarks; developing a project risk and mitigation plan, handling all logistical and administrative requirements and exemptions necessary for smooth project implementation and setting up the monitoring and evaluation system. - This phase would pursue the case study, action-learning, and networking components in parallel. Implementation phaseImplementation of the anticipated follow-up project (component 2) is estimated to take four years (July 2021 - December 2025). The outputs of activities for component one (the inception phase) will determine the extent and scope of the second phase of the Project. Hence, the detailed activities needing external funding will be further defined after the end of the first phase.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Water Resources Management for Water Sanitation and Hygiene is a Market-based approachThe project will be implemented in Ethiopia, focusing on the water catchment areas surrounding Addis Ababa in the Oromia Regional State. It will specifically target the four main surface water supply sources for Addis Ababa: the Legedadi, Gefersa, Dire, and Akaki catchments, along with their associated reservoirs. Additionally, the project will extend to five nearby towns within and around these catchment areas: Akaki, Burayu, Gelan, Sululta, and Sendafa.</narrative>
  </description>
